Which validation step stopped, whether it stopped or threw, and which integrity check refused.

SecStaticCodeCheckValidity was already known to be where MoneyMoney sat. These are the steps it is
made of, one line each, plus the two things that made the earlier readings wrong.

FIRST, THE CATCH BLOCKS PRINT TOO. A call line with no back line means hung OR THREW, and I read it
as hung for a whole rung. validateNonResourceComponents had not blocked at all.

SECOND, checkIntegrity threw the same errSecCSSignatureFailed from nine different places, so the
status alone said only that the blob was refused, never why. Each one names itself now.

WHAT THEY FOUND, and it is not the application:

    CIDER_CSSTEP validateDirectory call
    CIDER_CSSTEP verifySignature call
    CIDER_CSSTEP CMS signer status=3 (kCMSSignerInvalidSignature)
    CIDER_CSSTEP core threw MacOSError error=-67061

No CIDER_CDIR line, so the CodeDirectory blob itself is structurally fine; it is the CMS signature
over it that we judge invalid. THE PROBE CARRIED ITS OWN CONTROL and the control fired: the same
question asked of iTerm.app and LibreOffice.app in the same container gives the IDENTICAL answer,
three bundles of three. So this is our CMS verification refusing every third-party signature, not
anything about the bundle MoneyMoney ships.

